 ### SAS game record log
 
-`SASGameRecord_*.log` is a separate compact game record for autoplay and AI-strength review. It gives high-level context such as initial map/landmass geography and resource/yield context, economy, expansion, city and battle history, autoplay start/end, player appearance/elimination, run status, worked plots, unit composition, diplomacy, exploration, environmental and map changes, project-victory progress, and game state, which is useful on its own and also helps an LLM interpret detailed BBAI decision traces.
+`SASGameRecord_*.log` is a separate compact game record for autoplay and AI-strength review. It gives high-level context such as initial map/landmass geography and bonus/yield context, economy, expansion, city and battle history, autoplay start/end, player appearance/elimination, run status, worked plots, unit composition including `UnitCombat` shares, diplomacy, exploration, environmental and map changes, project-victory progress, compact air/missile/nuclear posture and per-city air-base capacity, and game state, which is useful on its own and also helps an LLM interpret detailed BBAI decision traces.
 
 Free-text values such as city, player, leader, civ, map-script, and log-file names are quoted and escaped so names with spaces remain parser-friendly. It is currently an all-player diagnostic record and can contain spoilers, so it is not a spoiler-free player-advice export.

