+## 197.7 - (Fixed/Improved) Base AdvCiv/K-Mod early building short-circuit (`CvCityAI::AI_chooseProduction`'s short-circuit 1) ignored BuildUnitProb and could start fresh infrastructure despite maximum military-production pressure
+
+The continued KI#197 military-production investigation exposed another inherited asymmetry in `CvCityAI::AI_chooseProduction`. The early building-value short-circuit ("short-circuit 1") calculates a small chance to take the current best building before most later production logic, but unlike short-circuit 2 and the KI#197.2-corrected short-circuit 3, its building chance did not use the already-computed `iBuildUnitProb`. As a result, even an AI whose normal military-production pressure had reached `BuildUnitProb=100` could still randomly start fresh infrastructure before reaching the military choices that the same production routine was otherwise strongly requesting.
+
+Save file 454 made this visible once the BBAI military-production trace also recorded building production already invested. In the pre-fix run, short-circuit 1 chose a building in 10 of 70 evaluations with `BuildUnitProb=100`, and 6 of those choices started from 0 production. Birka alone started a fresh Jewish Temple on turn 146, Forge on turn 250, Jail on turn 255, Jewish Monastery on turn 259, another Jewish Temple on turn 264 and Factory on turn 276. The turn-255 example was especially clear: Scandinavia had 9 cities, 52 military units, substantial military-spending headroom and a +45% relative-understrength catch-up; Birka's `BuildUnitProb` had reached 100, yet the inherited 4% short-circuit 1 roll still started a new Jail at 0/99 production.
+
+AdvCiv-SAS now lets the already-computed military pressure reduce only short-circuit 1's base building odds while the normal `max+15` military-spending allowance still permits another unit. `SAS_AI_CHOOSE_PRODUCTION_SHORT_CIRCUIT_1_BUILD_UNIT_PROB_WEIGHT_PERCENT`, 100 by default, controls the strength: with the default value, `BuildUnitProb=80` reduces the gate's base building odds by 80%, and `BuildUnitProb=100` reduces them to 0. The inherited production-progress preference inside `AI_chooseBuilding` is deliberately unchanged, so an important building already underway can still win on continuity. The spending threshold is only a permission gate for applying military pressure, not a target army size: being below it does not by itself force the AI to build units, and once unit spending is already above `max+15`, the inherited short-circuit 1 odds are left unchanged. Setting the define to 0 restores the Base AdvCiv/K-Mod short-circuit 1 odds.
+
+The confirming save-file 454 rerun logged 4,963 short-circuit 1 evaluations. There were 213 evaluations with `BuildUnitProb=100`; 211 still had military-spending room, and 209 of those rejected the building. The only two successful `BuildUnitProb=100` choices were continuity cases: Nidaros continued a Levee already at 81/162 production (50%) and later an Airport already at 79/225 production (about 35%). No fresh building won short-circuit 1 at `BuildUnitProb=100` while spending room remained. A direct turn-160 example showed the intended production flow: Nidaros was in a land/total war with `BuildUnitProb=100`, 95 unit spending against a 299 maximum and a fresh Granary valued highly enough for 23% inherited short-circuit 1 odds; the new rule reduced those base odds to 0, and after the later normal gates the city selected a Crossbowman instead.
+
+The rerun diverged strategically from the pre-fix game history, so later total army sizes are not treated as a controlled A/B measurement of this one change. The local production traces do directly confirm the intended effect: fresh infrastructure no longer randomly overrides maximum military-production pressure at this early gate, while already-invested buildings retain their inherited completion advantage and later building opportunities remain available.
+
+Fixed/improved with the help of GPT-5.6 Thinking thanks.

