 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6047+) **AI armies no longer wait indefinitely in one city while preparing only for Barbarian conquest:** SASGameRecord and BBAI logging in save file 453 showed an unfinished Base AdvCiv rule in `CvUnitAI::AI_attackCityMove`, amplified by K-Mod grouping `AI_omniGroup`, kept armies assembled to capture a Barbarian city waiting merely because they had grown larger than needed for their weak target; for example, when the estimated Barbarian garrison was two units and five attackers were otherwise enough, those five could move, but adding a sixth made the entire army "not ready" again. While the army waited, normal grouping kept sending additional units into it, making it even larger and preventing those units from defending elsewhere or forming another expedition. In save file 453, individual waiting groups reached 65-82% of an empire's military - up to 201 units - while the AI paid their upkeep and delayed conquering reachable weak Barbarian cities. To fix this, the AI now divides such an army once into several self-sufficient expeditions that can capture different Barbarian cities, defend territory, or prepare for later wars, and prevents them from immediately joining back together. Normal large armies remain allowed during active wars and when a planned surprise attack is ready. See [KI#188](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#188---fixedimproved-major-base-advcivk-mod-bug-in-organizing-armies-against-barbarian-cities-could-park-65-82-of-an-ais-military-or-prevent-capable-attackers-from-forming-city-assault-expeditions).
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6047+) **Capable early armies can organize themselves to capture Barbarian cities:** SASGameRecord and BBAI logging also found AIs with 9-14 units individually able (`UNITAI_ATTACK`) to attack and capture cities, but none assigned to organize the others (`UNITAI_ATTACK_CITY`) into a city-assault army, so this is a difference in `UNITAI` assignment, not their abilities. A K-Mod rule automatically broke down any group of 4 or more such units into smaller groups of 2 or 3 units if the group was in territory owned by the AI or one of its teammates. Because of this, many of the AI's military units could remain at home instead of grouping together to capture a reachable Barbarian city. To fix this, if no city the unit can reach within one turn needs it as a defender and the unit is not currently threatened, the AI now checks if enough attackers are available in the area, and if so, the AI assigns that unit as the expedition leader; the others can then group with it and they set out against a Barbarian city. For example, the save file 453 confirming run created four such expedition leaders. Among them, one was of a Spanish Chariot reassigned on T60 had gathered a four-unit group by T61, redirected toward Minoan on T73, and Spain captured it on T77. Another was of a War Elephant reassigned for the Holy Roman Empire on T79 was leading four units toward Khoisan by T86, and the Holy Roman Empire captured it on T90. See [KI#188](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#188---fixedimproved-major-base-advcivk-mod-bug-in-organizing-armies-against-barbarian-cities-could-park-65-82-of-an-ais-military-or-prevent-capable-attackers-from-forming-city-assault-expeditions).
